WEBVTT

00:00.720 --> 00:02.520
The Generation of Miracles.

00:02.520 --> 00:06.150
A dream team of five players that appear only once a decade.

00:06.150 --> 00:10.440
A phantom sixth man whom they regarded as their full teammate,

00:10.440 --> 00:12.300
Kuroko Tetsuya,

00:12.300 --> 00:14.990
and a power forward from America,

00:14.990 --> 00:16.820
Kagami Taiga.

00:16.820 --> 00:18.990
Thanks to the addition of these two rookies,

00:18.990 --> 00:23.080
Seirin High's basketball team is steadily advancing in the playoffs.

00:23.080 --> 00:25.540
We soundly defeated Kaijo High,

00:26.020 --> 00:29.550
and one of the Miracles, Kise Ryota, in a practice game.

00:29.550 --> 00:32.090
Then came Shutoku and another Miracle,

00:32.590 --> 00:37.140
ace shooter Midorima Shintaro,
in the finals of the Inter-High prelims.

00:37.140 --> 00:39.740
Combining their newly discovered talents,

00:39.740 --> 00:43.850
Kagami and Kuroko came from behind to beat Midorima's firestorm of three-pointers.

00:44.450 --> 00:47.950
We have finally made it to the championship league,

00:47.950 --> 00:50.020
the last set of games before the Inter-High.

00:51.020 --> 00:52.040
However...

00:53.460 --> 00:55.440
we had a new crisis on our hands.

00:55.490 --> 00:59.740
Kuroko's

00:55.490 --> 00:59.740
Basketball

00:55.530 --> 00:59.740
Idiots Never Win!

01:00.660 --> 01:01.700
God,

01:01.700 --> 01:04.210
what does our coach want <i>this</i> time?

01:04.670 --> 01:07.650
Now she's telling us to bring her our midterms.

01:07.650 --> 01:09.960
I hope she's not planning anything dumb.

01:10.350 --> 01:11.340
Who knows?

01:11.340 --> 01:14.880
But I've heard you can't go to the Inter-High if you're failing.

01:14.880 --> 01:16.840
Y-You're kidding!

01:16.840 --> 01:19.180
Hey, Kuroko! Kagami!

01:20.350 --> 01:24.320
Furihata, Kawahara, and, uh... Fukuda!

01:24.320 --> 01:26.850
I'm sure glad you remember our names.

01:27.680 --> 01:29.800
So why do this now?

01:29.800 --> 01:33.470
The finals are still a long ways off. Isn't it too soon?

01:33.470 --> 01:37.050
It might be related to the proficiency tests we have in two days.

01:37.050 --> 01:40.300
But the proficiency tests won't be counted on our grades.

01:40.300 --> 01:41.990
Oh, is that right?

01:42.650 --> 01:44.700
Then what's the problem?

01:45.580 --> 01:47.870
We should be practicing instead.

01:48.890 --> 01:50.880
We have a <i>huge</i> problem.

01:50.880 --> 01:53.370
Now I'm freaked out.

01:53.370 --> 01:57.210
As you all know, you have your proficiency tests in two days.

01:57.210 --> 01:59.950
Of course, your grades won't be affected.

01:59.950 --> 02:00.970
However...

02:01.420 --> 02:04.360
Our school has around 300 students per grade,

02:04.360 --> 02:06.430
and they will all be ranked.

02:06.430 --> 02:09.940
The worst 100 students will have to take remedial classes next Saturday.

02:09.940 --> 02:11.520
And there lies the problem.

02:12.620 --> 02:15.060
Saturday... during the championship league?

02:15.060 --> 02:18.090
You got it. You can't play if you bomb the test.

02:18.090 --> 02:20.160
This is not about winning or losing anymore.

02:20.540 --> 02:21.900
Now I get it.

02:22.370 --> 02:26.760
Because of that, if we think you're a risk based on your midterms,

02:26.760 --> 02:29.370
you'll be cramming at our coach's house starting tonight.

02:30.410 --> 02:31.960
The coach's house?

02:31.960 --> 02:34.040
We're just studying...

02:34.040 --> 02:35.730
nothing more.

02:36.650 --> 02:42.530
Any idiots who might not play next Saturday should not expect any "hijinks" tonight.

02:44.720 --> 02:47.310
Coach, you're scaring the first years.

02:47.730 --> 02:50.650
All right, let's see those tests.

02:54.880 --> 02:55.730
Here.

02:55.730 --> 02:56.610
Thanks.

02:58.650 --> 03:03.680
Furihata, Kawahara, and Fukuda... I think you're all in the clear.

03:03.680 --> 03:05.840
But study up, just in case.

03:05.840 --> 03:06.670
Sure thing!

03:06.670 --> 03:08.160
Thank God.

03:08.820 --> 03:10.500
Up next we have...

03:10.990 --> 03:12.390
‘Sup.

03:12.390 --> 03:12.960
Here.

03:13.500 --> 03:18.460
Perfect, the two invaluable players who are also the least predictable.

03:18.830 --> 03:21.800
Yet the future of Seirin basketball rides on their shoulders.

03:22.860 --> 03:24.890
First we'll see what Kuroko got.

03:24.890 --> 03:24.930
Chemistry

03:24.890 --> 03:24.930
Math

03:24.890 --> 03:24.930
Biology

03:25.100 --> 03:25.140
Japanese

03:25.100 --> 03:25.140
Answer Sheet

03:26.180 --> 03:26.220
English

03:26.810 --> 03:26.850
History

03:28.350 --> 03:31.350
Wow, so average.

03:31.770 --> 03:33.200
N-Not that they're bad!

03:33.200 --> 03:34.680
But they're not all that good either.

03:34.680 --> 03:36.440
Oh, but he's good at Japanese.

03:36.440 --> 03:38.280
But it doesn't make him any less average.

03:38.730 --> 03:40.830
You got a 63 in Japanese History?

03:40.830 --> 03:43.450
Kuroko, are you really that smart?

03:44.380 --> 03:46.620
Oh, god. I should've known.

03:46.620 --> 03:47.740
Here.

03:52.290 --> 03:52.420
World History

03:54.080 --> 03:55.130
These suck!

03:55.130 --> 03:58.840
I knew you were a moron! But I never you were this big of a moron!

03:58.840 --> 04:02.090
And he actually got a zero, which is amazing in itself!

04:02.090 --> 04:04.550
Why are you so bad at English?!

04:04.550 --> 04:07.040
I thought you were raised in America.

04:07.040 --> 04:09.800
Japanese English is too damn analytical!

04:09.800 --> 04:12.940
You just say what you want, long as people understand you!

04:12.940 --> 04:13.940
Who said

04:13.940 --> 04:17.350
you had any right to complain?!

04:18.750 --> 04:20.190
Wow...

04:20.190 --> 04:23.220
We'll all have to pitch in to help him cram.

04:24.000 --> 04:27.780
Are you all smart enough to teach me stuff... sirs?

04:27.780 --> 04:29.440
Don't doubt us!

04:30.250 --> 04:31.690
Of course we are!

04:31.690 --> 04:33.540
We're smarter than you!

04:33.540 --> 04:38.280
Allow me to announce what these guys received in the last proficiency tests!

04:38.280 --> 04:41.950
First is our captain, Hyuga Junpei! He ranked 112th out of 305!

04:41.950 --> 04:43.730
I'd say it's about right.

04:43.730 --> 04:45.590
Izuki Shun ranked 71st!

04:45.590 --> 04:48.230
Easier than drinking ice cocoa. Ooh, that was nice!

04:48.230 --> 04:51.650
...moving on, Tsuchida Satoshi ranked 81st!

04:51.650 --> 04:53.990
Mitobe Rinnosuke was 74th!

04:53.990 --> 04:56.740
And I, Koganei Shinji, was 52nd!

04:56.740 --> 04:58.260
Holy crap, guys!

04:58.260 --> 05:00.690
That goes especially for you, Koganei!

05:00.690 --> 05:03.990
Last but not least, our coach Aida Riko ranked second!

05:06.700 --> 05:10.410
Y-You were second? You're that smart?

05:10.410 --> 05:12.050
Guess so.

05:12.050 --> 05:14.800
But captain, I thought you'd be smarter since you wear glasses...

05:14.800 --> 05:17.340
Not everyone who wears glasses is smart!

05:17.340 --> 05:19.630
Besides, I had an above average score!

05:19.630 --> 05:23.090
God. Who needs grades if you can shoot hoops?

05:26.470 --> 05:29.890
Any idiot can "shoot hoops"! But...

05:29.890 --> 05:31.510
Idiots never win!

05:38.240 --> 05:42.740
Who needs grades if you can play basketball?

05:42.740 --> 05:47.600
That whole "you won't be a starter if you flunk this test" stuff was a lie, right?

05:47.600 --> 05:50.410
How uptight is our team anyway?

05:51.140 --> 05:52.780
I'm bored.

05:57.460 --> 06:01.670
Anyway, how'd you get so good at rock-paper-scissors?

06:04.460 --> 06:07.650
It is only because you're so bad at it, Takao.

06:07.650 --> 06:11.430
Oh yeah, we have those proficienct tests in two days. Are you studying?

06:11.430 --> 06:12.620
Of course I am.

06:12.620 --> 06:14.330
I do everything that is required of me.

06:14.330 --> 06:16.920
I'm bad at Japanese history.

06:16.920 --> 06:20.790
Fujiwara-no-Smoojiwara... all the names sound the same to me!

06:20.790 --> 06:24.530
You rely on rote memorization without understanding the content, fool.

06:24.530 --> 06:28.760
So... what do you think'll be on the test? Why don't you take a guess?

06:28.760 --> 06:29.990
Why should I?

06:29.990 --> 06:33.310
Today's horoscope said the luckiest sign is Cancer.

06:33.310 --> 06:34.750
Help me out here.

06:35.410 --> 06:37.190
Don't rely on others!

06:40.200 --> 06:41.210
We're here.

06:41.210 --> 06:43.290
So this is your room, Coach?

06:43.290 --> 06:45.950
It's more neat and girly than I imagined.

06:45.950 --> 06:47.680
Sit your stupid butt down, Kagami!

06:47.680 --> 06:49.130
"S-Stupid butt"?

06:52.970 --> 06:54.990
Let's begin our cram session.

06:54.990 --> 06:57.150
The proficiency tests cover five subjects.

06:57.150 --> 07:00.650
I've assembled a team of specialists in each of those subjects.

07:01.360 --> 07:03.360
A team of specialists?

07:03.360 --> 07:05.360
Mitobe will handle science.

07:05.980 --> 07:07.540
Kuroko has Japanese.

07:07.540 --> 07:09.370
So she says. Please prepare yourself.

07:09.370 --> 07:11.360
W-Why are <i>you</i> my tutor?

07:11.360 --> 07:12.960
Izuki has math.

07:12.960 --> 07:15.040
I put the "fun" in "functions." Ooh, classic!

07:15.040 --> 07:16.610
I can't deal with this dude!

07:16.610 --> 07:18.000
Hyuga has social studies.

07:18.000 --> 07:21.210
I'll beat the Sengoku Era into your head.

07:21.210 --> 07:23.500
That's too specific! And we haven't gotten to it yet!

07:23.500 --> 07:24.800
Tsuchida has English.

07:24.800 --> 07:27.330
You're teaching <i>me</i> English... sir?

07:27.330 --> 07:29.340
I got a 95 on it.

07:29.340 --> 07:30.280
And lastly...

07:30.280 --> 07:32.520
I will be supervising the whole thing.

07:32.520 --> 07:35.720
We're the team of specialists who'll make your stupid butt smarter!

07:36.160 --> 07:38.630
What about you, Koganei?

07:38.630 --> 07:41.280
I'm responsible for hitting you if you doze off.

07:41.280 --> 07:43.020
With this special slapstick!

07:43.020 --> 07:46.020
Koganei is neither good nor bad at any subjects.

07:46.020 --> 07:47.500
He's a true ungifted academic!

07:47.500 --> 07:48.690
Harsh.

07:50.710 --> 07:52.390
Number Two? Where'd he come from?

07:52.390 --> 07:56.650
Tetsuya Two will be our guard dog that'll make sure you don't escape.

07:57.270 --> 07:59.200
Stay back! Go, get lost!

08:00.380 --> 08:03.760
Here's our two-day schedule!

08:01.330 --> 08:01.370
THE 17TH

08:01.620 --> 08:01.660
STUDY

08:02.000 --> 08:02.040
SCHOOL

08:02.000 --> 08:02.040
TEST

08:02.080 --> 08:02.120
3 PM

08:02.120 --> 08:02.170
9 AM

08:02.250 --> 08:02.290
12 PM

08:02.580 --> 08:02.620
SCHOOL
(STUDY)

08:03.000 --> 08:03.040
THE 15TH
6 PM

08:04.970 --> 08:07.300
Wait! When do I sleep?!

08:07.300 --> 08:10.090
He will literally be up day and night until the test, won't he?

08:09.050 --> 08:09.090
THE 16TH

08:10.090 --> 08:13.630
But I heard that all-nighters are actually not very efficient...

08:13.630 --> 08:15.850
You're the last person to talk about "efficiency"!

08:15.840 --> 08:19.090
Complete
Both

08:16.180 --> 08:19.100
You wrote that word down as "bear graduation" on the writing test!

08:19.100 --> 08:20.640
Man, you're thorough.

08:20.640 --> 08:23.400
Staying up for two days won't kill anyone.

08:23.400 --> 08:25.310
All right, first we'll do math!

08:25.310 --> 08:27.900
Come! Let's do a Sine, Cosine, Cossack Dance!

08:27.900 --> 08:29.470
Learn the formulas by moving our bodies!

08:29.470 --> 08:31.310
I can't deal with this guy!

08:31.310 --> 08:32.220
Hey!

08:32.220 --> 08:33.620
Get off me!

08:33.620 --> 08:34.510
Mitobe, hold him!

08:34.510 --> 08:36.380
I wanna go home!

08:41.600 --> 08:43.170
What do you call organisms

08:43.170 --> 08:47.370
that neither has an endoskeleton nor an exoskeleton, like octopi or slugs?

08:47.370 --> 08:48.660
Spineless animals.

08:48.660 --> 08:51.290
You're wrong. The correct answer is "mollusks."

08:51.290 --> 08:52.250
Next question:

08:52.250 --> 08:58.790
An organism called a planarian, which is a fellow invertebrate like the mollusks, has incredible regenerative abilities.

08:58.790 --> 09:01.220
But what happens if you cut one up into eight equal parts?

09:01.220 --> 09:02.110
It'll die.

09:02.110 --> 09:02.600
You're wrong.

09:02.600 --> 09:05.940
The hell I am! You're cutting it into pieces! That's a death sentence!

09:05.940 --> 09:09.960
No, each piece will regenerate, and you'll get eight separate planarians.

09:09.960 --> 09:11.830
No you won't!

09:11.830 --> 09:14.650
Besides, who gives a rat's ass about planarians?

09:14.650 --> 09:17.580
Saying that will spell the end for you, Kagami.

09:17.580 --> 09:19.350
Please calm down.

09:19.350 --> 09:21.320
You put me through the gauntlet all night,

09:21.320 --> 09:24.480
and now you're tossing off questions while walking to school?

09:24.480 --> 09:25.750
You trying to kill me?

09:25.750 --> 09:28.340
We weren't done tutoring you on Mitobe's subject.

09:31.030 --> 09:31.870
Excuse me...

09:37.780 --> 09:39.310
Holy crap!

09:39.310 --> 09:40.390
Are you okay?

09:42.140 --> 09:43.760
Seriously...

09:43.760 --> 09:46.850
Forget the championship league, will I even make it to the test?

09:48.080 --> 09:49.310
I wonder too.

09:49.650 --> 09:50.710
Kagami...

09:51.640 --> 09:52.640
Fight for it.

09:53.520 --> 09:55.220
Damn you, Kuroko.

09:55.220 --> 09:56.780
You're enjoying this, aren't you?

09:57.560 --> 09:58.660
No, I'm not.

10:09.720 --> 10:11.650
Is it lunchtime already?

10:11.650 --> 10:13.350
Gotta fill my stomach!

10:14.510 --> 10:15.500
Kagami!

10:16.540 --> 10:17.440
Izuki.

10:17.440 --> 10:20.940
We're spending lunchtime in the library doing factors.

10:20.940 --> 10:23.210
Oh, can we factor in some of that lunch?

10:23.210 --> 10:24.730
Whoa! That was sweet!

10:27.000 --> 10:29.000
Now I want to kill him.

10:29.000 --> 10:31.160
I don't think he has any ill intent.

10:31.160 --> 10:35.200
In fact, everybody is doing this because they need you.

10:35.200 --> 10:37.320
I know that, but...

10:39.510 --> 10:44.790
Idiots can't play in the championship league,
let alone the Inter-High.

10:44.790 --> 10:49.250
We said we wanted to beat the Miracles and become the top team in Japan.

10:49.630 --> 10:54.920
So this is no time to slip up...
Not with three more to beat! Dammit!

11:17.070 --> 11:21.000
We need you in order to beat them, Kagami.

11:36.640 --> 11:38.300
Midorimacchi!

11:38.810 --> 11:40.400
You are being too loud.

11:40.400 --> 11:41.510
What do you want, Kise?

11:41.920 --> 11:43.830
Kise? You mean the one from Kaijo?

11:43.830 --> 11:46.800
Do you still have that thing? I really need it!

11:46.800 --> 11:47.740
What thing?

11:47.740 --> 11:50.600
You know, that secret weapon for acing tests!

11:50.600 --> 11:53.020
What is wrong with you people?

11:53.020 --> 11:57.350
Lucky items are only beneficial to those who do what is required of them.

11:57.350 --> 11:59.530
It is not for those who rely on others.

11:59.530 --> 12:02.950
Gosh, you're mean! My starting position's on the—

12:03.660 --> 12:05.000
Midorimacchi!

12:05.000 --> 12:08.330
Oh man, I'm in huge trouble!

12:08.330 --> 12:11.290
Oh yeah, Kurokocchi must have one!

12:11.290 --> 12:12.710
Kurokocchi

12:11.290 --> 12:11.870
DIAL

12:12.120 --> 12:12.250
END

12:18.670 --> 12:18.800
CALL ENDED

12:20.030 --> 12:21.150
Who's that?

12:21.150 --> 12:21.840
No one.

12:22.440 --> 12:24.150
Someone must have dialed the wrong number.

12:28.760 --> 12:31.830
He definitely ended that call himself!

12:31.830 --> 12:34.480
That's mean, Kurokocchi!

12:37.780 --> 12:38.870
Kagami.

12:38.870 --> 12:39.650
Huh?

12:40.150 --> 12:41.690
This is the last resort.

12:41.690 --> 12:43.860
If everything else fails, use this.

12:46.320 --> 12:47.840
What's this?

12:47.840 --> 12:49.160
It got numbers on it.

12:48.580 --> 12:53.080
0
This pencil reads, 'Yutori Tenjin,' on top, and, 'Do everything that's required and leave the rest to fate,' in the middle.

12:49.650 --> 12:52.330
Midorima gave that to me in middle school.

12:52.330 --> 12:56.340
It's a pencil roller made out of a Yutori Tenjin Shrine pencil.

12:56.340 --> 12:59.170
I don't need this thing!

13:02.330 --> 13:03.440
What the hell?!

13:03.440 --> 13:05.300
It'll attack you if you defy it.

13:11.680 --> 13:14.470
So you <i>do</i> have a secret weapon.

13:14.470 --> 13:17.260
If it's so good, then let me have it.

13:17.260 --> 13:19.850
You're smart anyway, so you don't need it.

13:19.850 --> 13:20.900
I refuse to.

13:21.360 --> 13:25.570
I make it a point to prepare for any and all occasions.

13:31.760 --> 13:33.790
No, you've got it all wrong!

13:33.790 --> 13:35.470
Look at this figure!

13:35.470 --> 13:37.440
This is Maeda Toshiie!

13:37.440 --> 13:40.270
I thought the one holding the spear was Toshiie.

13:40.270 --> 13:41.090
Moron!

13:41.090 --> 13:44.160
Yes, he wields a spear, but that's Sanada Yukimura!

13:44.160 --> 13:47.720
Look at his flag! It has the Rokumonsen, the family crest!

13:50.140 --> 13:53.330
For the next one, which one is Uesugi Kenshin?

13:53.330 --> 13:55.050
Let's see...

13:55.050 --> 13:56.600
Excuse me.

13:57.150 --> 13:59.560
I don't believe that'll be on the test.

13:59.560 --> 14:01.360
Whether it does or not depends on luck!

14:02.030 --> 14:06.590
Gosh, Koganei! It doesn't help if the guard is sleeping!

14:06.590 --> 14:08.110
I think I've also...

14:08.110 --> 14:10.230
reached my limit.

14:11.920 --> 14:18.920
Operation Make the Kagamidiot Smarter!

14:12.510 --> 14:15.990
It <i>is</i> getting late, and you guys must be hungry.

14:15.990 --> 14:18.920
Fine, I'll go make us a midnight snack.

14:18.920 --> 14:20.830
Our coach's midnight snack?!

14:21.470 --> 14:22.710
N-No, that's fine!

14:22.710 --> 14:24.800
I'll go to the convenience store!

14:24.800 --> 14:28.960
And Number Two look like he needs a walk, so he can tag along!

14:28.960 --> 14:30.550
Kagami, you have Japanese next.

14:31.300 --> 14:32.140
Sure.

14:32.140 --> 14:33.870
Let's go, Number Two!

14:36.660 --> 14:37.560
Bye.

14:40.150 --> 14:41.520
What was that about?

14:44.740 --> 14:48.820
The sun's coming up. So the tests'll start in three hours, right?

14:50.380 --> 14:53.150
I had him do questions from last year's tests.

14:53.150 --> 14:54.000
How'd he do?

14:54.000 --> 14:55.260
Not good enough.

14:55.260 --> 14:58.790
He's simply not improving in one subject: Japanese.

14:59.240 --> 15:02.750
Forgive me. There's nothing more I can do about it.

15:03.120 --> 15:04.760
Okay, here's what we'll do:

15:04.760 --> 15:06.520
Japanese is out. Dropped.

15:07.600 --> 15:10.740
Each question on the test has four multiple-choice answers.

15:10.740 --> 15:13.430
Even if he answers randomly, he should still get around 25%.

15:13.790 --> 15:16.390
I guess it makes sense statistically.

15:16.390 --> 15:18.870
We'll make it up with the other four subjects!

15:18.870 --> 15:20.270
That's our only choice!

15:21.290 --> 15:23.780
I'm back! I got us something.

15:23.780 --> 15:24.360
Huh?

15:24.940 --> 15:26.070
Where's Kagami?

15:26.500 --> 15:28.980
Huh? He said he was going to the bathroom.

15:28.980 --> 15:32.530
Uh, I was just out front. The bathroom light was off.

15:32.880 --> 15:35.490
Wait, don't tell me! Kagami...

15:37.250 --> 15:38.580
Escaped?!

15:38.580 --> 15:39.980
What's that?

15:39.980 --> 15:41.680
This is my time to shine!

15:41.680 --> 15:43.410
But you were the one asleep at your post!

15:43.410 --> 15:44.710
Let's go, Number Two!

15:44.710 --> 15:46.800
Track him down and bag him!

15:46.800 --> 15:48.750
Let's move out!

15:48.750 --> 15:49.870
Yeah!

15:54.430 --> 15:56.770
You guys are enjoying this.

15:58.160 --> 16:00.070
Hey, wait up!

16:04.940 --> 16:07.920
Number Two, wait for us! You're too fast!

16:07.920 --> 16:09.780
Where is he going?

16:09.780 --> 16:12.330
I know the way Kagami thinks.

16:12.330 --> 16:14.170
We're heading towards Maji Burger!

16:14.170 --> 16:15.320
You're right!

16:15.320 --> 16:18.390
He must have left to feed his huge, starving frame!

16:18.390 --> 16:20.120
Are you sure?

16:20.770 --> 16:24.360
Kagami knows you guys are counting on him.

16:24.360 --> 16:26.590
I don't believe he would escape.

16:29.130 --> 16:30.550
Where is he going?

16:30.550 --> 16:32.760
I'm sure this way leads to...

16:37.680 --> 16:40.490
Wait, isn't this the street basketball court?

16:40.490 --> 16:42.060
And there's someone here.

16:42.640 --> 16:43.890
Is that...

16:48.270 --> 16:49.940
That jackass.

16:50.500 --> 16:54.620
We told him several times he can't play basketball if he flunks the test!

16:54.620 --> 16:58.230
I don't believe this. He really is an idiot to the core.

16:58.230 --> 17:00.170
No, hold on a second.

17:00.170 --> 17:01.660
He seems to be shouting something.

17:01.660 --> 17:03.910
Sine! Cosine! Tangent!

17:05.080 --> 17:07.790
Here He Lies Beneath Bed Clothes!

17:08.160 --> 17:09.570
In 794, the old capital was...

17:09.570 --> 17:10.750
built before!

17:21.150 --> 17:23.270
What do you think you're doing?

17:23.270 --> 17:25.440
Is this your way of studying?

17:25.820 --> 17:30.900
Well, my true nature was getting in the way of all that sucky cramming.

17:31.540 --> 17:35.360
So I thought shooting hoops might help me learn better.

17:35.360 --> 17:36.660
I get it now.

17:36.660 --> 17:40.530
Even Izuki said I should move my body.

17:42.540 --> 17:46.500
Anyways, I'll definitely play next Saturday.

17:47.190 --> 17:48.350
Kagami...

17:48.350 --> 17:51.630
God, I can't even get angry at you.

17:51.630 --> 17:52.700
Me neither.

17:52.700 --> 17:56.170
All right! Final stretch, gang! Let's go for broke!

17:56.170 --> 17:58.010
We'll help you out, Kagami!

17:59.670 --> 18:00.810
Thanks!

18:00.810 --> 18:02.670
Wait a minute, your legs!

18:06.180 --> 18:09.050
You're still injured from the Shutoku game!

18:09.050 --> 18:11.200
Oh yeah...

18:12.650 --> 18:14.390
Irregular conjugation of "su" verbs!

18:14.390 --> 18:16.950
Uh... se, shi, su! Suru, sure, seyo!

18:20.160 --> 18:22.500
This is so boring, I can't retain it!

18:22.500 --> 18:24.430
At least you're holding a ball!

18:24.430 --> 18:25.370
Um...

18:26.260 --> 18:29.330
Se, shi, su! Suru, sure, seyo!

18:32.290 --> 18:35.260
Turn Off Mobile Devices

18:32.290 --> 18:35.260
No Chit-Chat

18:32.290 --> 18:35.260
Proficiency Test

18:35.760 --> 18:39.430
Even with all that cramming, it's just as I predicted.

18:39.430 --> 18:44.220
I won't get enough points in the last four subjects to make up for one!

18:44.220 --> 18:49.190
And this last one is my worst subject ever: Japanese!

18:49.190 --> 18:54.140
"Which one of these four choices best describes how the hero feels"?

18:54.140 --> 18:55.680
How would I know?!

18:55.680 --> 18:59.330
We'd all have it easy if we knew each other's feelings!

19:00.070 --> 19:03.160
No! You've worked too hard to quit now!

19:03.620 --> 19:06.570
Shutoku Private High School

19:09.520 --> 19:10.720
What's this?

19:10.720 --> 19:13.230
Normally "C" would be the right answer,

19:13.230 --> 19:15.700
but I've already answered "C" five times in a row.

19:15.700 --> 19:18.510
This is too strange to be a coincidence.

19:18.510 --> 19:20.110
No, remain calm.

19:20.110 --> 19:22.760
You will be correct to rely on your instincts.

19:22.760 --> 19:25.260
But this array of answers...

19:25.260 --> 19:26.710
Is it a trap?

19:26.710 --> 19:28.110
If that's the case...

19:28.770 --> 19:32.680
I've done everything I could. This is purely for confirmation.

19:33.190 --> 19:33.230
1st Proficiency Test

19:33.900 --> 19:33.940
Borrowing it
for a sec!

19:40.260 --> 19:41.570
Next we have...

19:45.990 --> 19:49.960
Takao!

19:57.240 --> 19:58.350
Kagami.

19:58.350 --> 20:00.670
Kagami. Did you really...

20:00.670 --> 20:02.330
Shut up.

20:03.330 --> 20:06.810
All I could do was roll that stupid pencil.

20:06.810 --> 20:08.510
Is that so?

20:08.510 --> 20:10.360
I'm done for!

20:16.150 --> 20:17.730
The next day...

20:17.730 --> 20:21.120
Hurry up! The fate of our team is riding on this!

20:21.120 --> 20:22.790
Make us proud, Kagami!

20:22.790 --> 20:26.230
If you're in the bottom 100, you're dead to me!

20:26.230 --> 20:28.410
Kagami! How'd you do?!

20:39.500 --> 20:41.300
Out of

20:39.500 --> 20:41.300
Students

20:42.620 --> 20:44.510
You're kidding! How?

20:45.000 --> 20:48.080
Forget the bottom 100, he made it into the top 100!

20:48.080 --> 20:49.000
What? Eh?

20:49.000 --> 20:50.970
You got a 98 in Japanese?!

20:50.980 --> 20:52.930
Average Score

20:50.980 --> 20:52.930
Score

20:50.980 --> 20:52.930
Subject

20:52.930 --> 20:55.720
So how did you do it?

20:55.720 --> 20:56.400
Well...

20:57.000 --> 20:59.400
all I did was roll that pencil.

21:00.400 --> 21:02.320
Huh? A pencil?

21:02.950 --> 21:05.910
What's this? Yutori Tenjin?

21:05.910 --> 21:08.530
It's a pencil roller made by Midorima.

21:08.530 --> 21:10.860
And you got a 98 with this?

21:10.860 --> 21:12.540
That Midorima's freaky!

21:13.170 --> 21:18.500
Say what you will, but at least nobody has to take remedial classes.

21:18.840 --> 21:21.090
Yeah, thank god for that.

21:21.090 --> 21:24.490
Let's set our sights on winning the championship league!

21:24.490 --> 21:25.830
Yeah!

21:27.960 --> 21:29.050
Huh?

21:29.580 --> 21:31.380
What's wrong, Hyuga?

21:31.380 --> 21:33.310
No way! You're crying?!

21:33.310 --> 21:36.830
I just... I can't believe I lost to Kagami!

21:37.680 --> 21:41.020
I'm not even an idiot!

21:41.020 --> 21:44.690
Uh, you know Kagami didn't earn it on his own.

21:44.690 --> 21:45.640
Right?

21:47.390 --> 21:49.450
Why are you crying too?

21:49.840 --> 21:53.190
I feel... like I've lost to Midorima.

21:54.640 --> 21:58.920
I can't believe I had to rely on that punk!

21:59.410 --> 22:01.140
Goddammit!

22:02.240 --> 22:04.420
Gosh, what is wrong with you people?

22:04.960 --> 22:06.730
I suggest that we leave them alone.

22:07.370 --> 22:09.390
Men have their pride, you know.

22:09.390 --> 22:12.370
You boys are such a chore.

22:13.390 --> 22:15.890
Why the hell?!

22:15.890 --> 22:17.200
Goddammit!

22:17.200 --> 22:19.980
You'll pay for this, Midorima!

22:37.630 --> 22:43.660
If this is what you want, go ahead and bare your fangs.

22:43.660 --> 22:49.780
Let them take the place of these fragile blue feelings.

22:50.550 --> 22:53.730
Hold steady, my brightest heart...

22:53.730 --> 22:56.770
We've shared joy and sorrow.

22:56.770 --> 23:01.840
You're the one who's always got my back with a smile.

23:03.370 --> 23:07.610
"Don't worry," I'll try to believe those words.

23:09.650 --> 23:15.380
I already know we can do this. I know we can win.

23:15.380 --> 23:18.440
'Cause he and I are one and the same!

23:18.440 --> 23:21.690
Let me higher! Get me higher!

23:21.690 --> 23:24.940
The fire inside me is burning bright.

23:24.940 --> 23:27.970
Even on this day like any other

23:27.970 --> 23:31.300
we're burnin' up, love, and believe.

23:31.300 --> 23:34.470
Rock me, baby. Show me, baby.

23:34.470 --> 23:37.190
Let's see more of what we can do.

23:37.190 --> 23:42.360
The way you and I are gonna create

23:38.890 --> 23:47.150
Saizen Fansubs Credits
Translation: kokujin-kun
Timing: ninjacloud
Editing: AMS
Typesetting: AMS
Karaoke: AMS
QC: sangofe, kokujin-kun, muyg
Encoding: Your Mom

23:42.360 --> 23:47.180
our legendary other selves.

24:00.330 --> 24:03.420
At long last, the Winter Cup begins!

24:03.420 --> 24:05.450
Kuroko, you ready?

24:05.450 --> 24:07.000
Yes, Kagami.

24:07.470 --> 24:10.010
But we're gonna have to get through the prelims first.

24:10.460 --> 24:11.970
I know!

24:11.970 --> 24:15.290
First, we'll beat all the members of the Generation of Miracles,

24:15.290 --> 24:16.760
and then we'll become the best in Japan!

24:17.190 --> 24:19.180
No matter how strong our opponents are,

24:19.180 --> 24:23.020
there's no way Seirin's going to lose!

24:23.800 --> 24:24.790
Kuroko's Basketball...

24:24.790 --> 24:26.710
Make sure you tune in!
